If you are using a DOS emulator on 64-bit windows in order to run a 32-
bit version of Nethack or Slash'EM, you should do the following in
order to get it to work:

1) Comment out the following line in your defaults.nh file by adding #
in front of it, as follows:
#OPTIONS=video:autodetect

2) Download and unzip the following file into the game's directory if
you are getting a DPMI error

http://www.delorie.com/djgpp/dl/ofc/simtel/v2misc/csdpmi5b.zip


I figured these changes out the hard way through trial and error, so I
hope I'll save some other people the hassle!


